WEBVTT

00:02.045 --> 00:03.296
[Man] Previously on lost:

00:03.379 --> 00:05.048
Can you hear me?

00:05.131 --> 00:08.760
Yes, yes, I can hear you.
Hey, are you on the boat?

00:08.843 --> 00:10.720
What boat? — your boat.

00:10.803 --> 00:12.764
I'm not on a boat. — uh...

00:12.847 --> 00:16.309
Naomi parachuted.
— who... who's Naomi?

00:16.392 --> 00:17.644
I've got it! I've got a signal!

00:17.727 --> 00:21.231
It's gonna work. It's happening.
We're gonna get off this island.

00:21.314 --> 00:22.398
[Wet thud]

00:25.485 --> 00:27.654
[Penny] Hello? Is Desmond there?

00:28.446 --> 00:29.489
Penny!

00:33.826 --> 00:37.413
I'm telling you, making that call
is the beginning of the end.

00:37.497 --> 00:40.166
Who is this?
— [man] Who is this?

00:42.085 --> 00:45.505
I'm one of the survivors
of oceanic flight 815.

00:46.965 --> 00:50.093
Can you get a fix on our location?
— sit tight.

00:50.176 --> 00:51.970
[Chatter]
— we'll be right there.

00:56.891 --> 01:00.019
[Waves crashing]
— [seagulls crying]

01:07.360 --> 01:10.071
[Sirens]

01:17.036 --> 01:18.454
[Tires screech]

01:20.832 --> 01:25.378
[Woman on TV] ...Almost 30 minutes since
the start of this high—speed chase.

01:25.461 --> 01:28.631
Still have no information
about who's driving this vehicle.

01:28.715 --> 01:31.718
Jeff, can you tell us
where the chase started?

01:31.801 --> 01:35.930
[Jeff] We're hearing reports that the
pursuit began near the la brea area,

01:36.014 --> 01:39.434
then traveled through a warehouse
district south of the 10 freeway.

01:39.517 --> 01:42.145
[Woman] Can you see how many people
are in the car?

01:42.228 --> 01:44.105
[Jeff] It appears to be just the driver.

01:44.188 --> 01:46.524
We're not sure if that's
the owner of the car.

01:46.607 --> 01:49.402
What you're seeing here
are pictures of the 10 freeway

01:49.485 --> 01:52.322
south of downtown.
— [woman] Is that a Camaro, Jeff?

01:52.405 --> 01:55.950
[Jeff] Yes, it looks like a vintage
early 703 model.

01:56.034 --> 01:57.034
Damn it.

01:57.076 --> 01:59.245
[Sirens]

02:05.418 --> 02:08.212
[Tires screech]

02:17.555 --> 02:19.265
Show us your hands!

02:20.767 --> 02:22.310
[Police radio chatter]

02:22.393 --> 02:24.187
[Helicopter]

02:24.270 --> 02:25.855
[Panting]

02:25.938 --> 02:29.067
Roll down the window
and show us your hands now!

02:39.202 --> 02:41.412
Slowly open the door
with your left hand.

02:49.087 --> 02:50.129
Get out of the car!

02:51.631 --> 02:53.466
Turn around, slow.

03:08.314 --> 03:09.649
On the ground!

03:18.658 --> 03:20.284
Stop! Don't you know who I am?

03:20.368 --> 03:24.455
Stop, wait! Don't you know who I am?
I'm one of the oceanic six!

03:25.665 --> 03:27.458
I'm one of the oceanic six!

03:43.975 --> 03:46.811
[Man] So five minutes
before you led ten cruisers

03:46.894 --> 03:48.688
on a chase across the city,

03:48.771 --> 03:51.983
you're minding your own business
in a convenience store?

03:52.692 --> 03:56.195
Until you see something and freak out.

03:57.029 --> 03:59.365
Mr. Reyes, why did you run like that?

03:59.449 --> 04:01.951
Who'd you see in there?

04:02.994 --> 04:05.788
Listen, buddy, I know you saw
somebody in that store

04:05.872 --> 04:09.125
that made you run away...
— wasn't running away from anyone.

04:09.208 --> 04:11.961
Do you think I care
that you're a celebrity?

04:12.044 --> 04:15.047
You crashed your Camaro
in the wrong neighborhood.

04:15.131 --> 04:17.383
I'm not a celebrity. — [scoffs]

04:18.301 --> 04:21.554
Is that why you kept shouting,
"hey, I'm one of the oceanic six"?

04:22.889 --> 04:25.391
You want to know a funny coincidence?

04:26.058 --> 04:27.059
Sure.

04:28.269 --> 04:30.146
I knew somebody on your plane.

04:31.355 --> 04:33.024
Really?

04:34.358 --> 04:36.611
Her name was Ana Lucia Cortez.

04:37.320 --> 04:40.448
She was my partner
before I made detective.

04:43.367 --> 04:45.369
Gorgeous.

04:47.747 --> 04:49.624
Maybe you knew her.

04:52.084 --> 04:56.047
Maybe met her on the plane,
before it took off?

04:58.049 --> 04:59.675
Sorry, never met her.

05:05.765 --> 05:08.434
Why don't you watch the tape?

05:09.060 --> 05:10.978
Maybe it'll spark something.

05:12.396 --> 05:14.023
I'm gonna get a doughnut.

05:14.106 --> 05:15.525
You want one?

05:16.442 --> 05:18.778
No, thanks. — when I come back,

05:18.861 --> 05:21.197
you're gonna tell me who you ran from.

05:53.688 --> 05:54.981
Help!

05:57.024 --> 05:58.568
Help!

05:58.651 --> 06:01.028
Help! Help me, help!

06:01.487 --> 06:03.864
What the hell is wrong with you?

06:03.948 --> 06:06.409
What are you doing, reyes?

06:06.492 --> 06:08.828
You trying to get tossed
into the nuthouse?

06:08.911 --> 06:12.415
Because if that's what you want I can
make that happen right now, my friend.

06:12.498 --> 06:13.916
You can?

06:14.458 --> 06:16.043
Oh, thank you.

06:16.127 --> 06:18.838
Thank you, thank you.

06:21.007 --> 06:24.635
Jack, you there, dude?
Beach to Jack. Come in, Jack.

06:25.678 --> 06:28.264
Beach to Jack.
— right here, Hurley. What's up?

06:28.347 --> 06:31.851
Hey, did you guys make it
to that radio tower thingy yet?

06:31.934 --> 06:34.437
Yeah. And I talked to the people
on the boat.

06:34.520 --> 06:36.814
They're on their way
to pick us up right now.

06:36.897 --> 06:39.191
Seriously? It worked?

06:39.275 --> 06:42.445
Seriously. We're all on the way
back to the beach right now,

06:42.528 --> 06:44.739
so you better pack your bags, buddy.

06:44.822 --> 06:48.451
[Laughing] Dude, that's great!

06:56.042 --> 06:58.628
Any luck?
— nothing, no sign of him.

06:58.711 --> 07:00.630
It's like he just disappeared.

07:01.881 --> 07:03.633
Why would Locke kill her?

07:03.716 --> 07:05.968
He hadn't met her.
— because he's crazy.

07:06.052 --> 07:07.887
So, what if he comes back?

07:07.970 --> 07:10.514
He comes back, I'm gonna kill him.

07:16.437 --> 07:18.314
I'm gonna get everybody together.

07:18.397 --> 07:20.650
Sooner we get back
to the beach the better.

07:24.070 --> 07:25.529
Are we really going home?

07:27.865 --> 07:29.575
Yeah, we're really going home.

07:35.956 --> 07:38.584
[Aaron cries] — [sun laughs]

07:38.668 --> 07:42.672
I can't believe I'm actually going
to have my baby in a hospital.

07:42.755 --> 07:44.507
Oh, rub it in, why don't you?

07:44.590 --> 07:47.343
Oh, no...
— you ladies need a hand?

07:47.426 --> 07:49.887
No, we're just
wrapping things up, thanks.

07:51.097 --> 07:55.685
You must be very proud of Bernard.
I hear he's quite the hero.

07:55.768 --> 07:58.854
Everyone up here knows
the real hero is your man, Claire.

07:58.938 --> 08:01.607
If Charlie didn't turn off that gizmo

08:01.691 --> 08:04.944
we'd still be getting a busy signal
on that fancy phone.

08:06.445 --> 08:10.866
So you better make sure you treat him
real good when we get back.

08:10.950 --> 08:12.952
Rose! — [Rose chuckles]

08:16.122 --> 08:17.748
Ok, thanks, I have enough.

08:17.832 --> 08:20.376
I need you to do me a favor.

08:22.461 --> 08:26.382
I need you to take Alex and
get as far from here as possible.

08:27.633 --> 08:29.635
Listen to me,
we don't have time for this.

08:29.719 --> 08:32.888
Everyone who stays here is going to die.

08:32.972 --> 08:35.850
Now get Alex and get away right now.

08:35.933 --> 08:38.227
I don't care where you go, just go.

08:38.310 --> 08:40.938
I will not have my daughter...

08:43.399 --> 08:45.776
She's not your daughter.

09:03.961 --> 09:06.172
Did I ever tell you iwon the lottery?

09:08.299 --> 09:13.053
I got, like, $150 million.
Worst thing that ever happened to me.

09:13.137 --> 09:15.598
Oh, yeah, who needs $150 million?

09:15.681 --> 09:19.477
Now it'll all be gone
'cause they all think I'm dead.

09:20.311 --> 09:23.314
When we get rescued and I go back...

09:24.565 --> 09:26.150
I'm gonna be free.

09:31.530 --> 09:32.948
I want to do a cannonball.

09:34.366 --> 09:38.037
I've been walking up and down
this beach every day

09:38.120 --> 09:41.665
and looking out at this water,
and I want to do a cannonball.

09:43.125 --> 09:46.086
Hurley, you want to do a cannonball?

09:46.712 --> 09:47.963
Cannonball.

10:34.426 --> 10:37.721
We need to get to Jack. We can't
let him get in touch with that boat.

10:37.805 --> 10:40.766
Easy, Scotty, everything's cool.
The boat's on the way.

10:40.850 --> 10:42.518
What? On the way? No.

10:42.601 --> 10:44.812
Where's Charlie?
— that woman Naomi lied.

10:44.895 --> 10:47.439
The people on the boat
aren't who they say they are!

10:47.523 --> 10:49.483
Then who are they?
— where's Charlie?

10:49.567 --> 10:52.027
I don't know, but we need
to get in touch with Jack now!

10:52.111 --> 10:54.530
We can call him, we have a walkie.
— get it!

10:54.613 --> 10:57.658
What do you mean people aren't who...?
— where's Charlie?!

11:04.081 --> 11:07.001
I'm... I'm sorry, brother. I...

11:27.479 --> 11:29.231
[Sat—phone rings]

11:31.817 --> 11:33.235
That's our ride.

11:35.237 --> 11:36.739
- — Hello?
- [Man] Hey, Jack.

11:36.822 --> 11:40.284
This is George minkowski. We're
trying to get a lock on your signal,

11:40.367 --> 11:42.453
but we're getting some rf interference.

11:42.536 --> 11:45.581
We're gonna need to rejigger
some settings on your sat—phone.

11:45.664 --> 11:47.875
Uh, sure. Ok,
just tell me what I gotta do.

11:47.958 --> 11:49.960
How about you put Naomi on?

11:50.836 --> 11:53.255
Naomi went to get some firewood.

11:53.339 --> 11:56.133
Can you hold on for a second?
Let me see if I can...

12:10.064 --> 12:11.357
Where is she?

12:14.193 --> 12:15.819
[Mutters]

12:21.283 --> 12:22.576
We gotta call the doc.

12:23.243 --> 12:26.080
Did you listen to Desmond?
Charlie wrote on his hand...

12:26.163 --> 12:28.165
Look, I'm sorry he's dead.

12:28.248 --> 12:30.709
But, I don't even know what
"not penny's boat" means.

12:30.793 --> 12:33.796
Calling Jack accomplishes nothing.
— It would warn him.

12:33.879 --> 12:37.132
It also warns the people on
the freighter we're suspicious of them.

12:37.216 --> 12:39.593
They're monitoring our communications.
If we call...

12:39.677 --> 12:42.221
You know what?
I got the walkie, I'm making the call.

12:42.304 --> 12:43.889
Hey! Give...

12:49.186 --> 12:51.188
We better get going.

12:55.901 --> 12:57.236
Going where?

13:03.450 --> 13:05.744
I found blood. The girl's trail.

13:05.828 --> 13:07.121
Probably crawled away.

13:07.204 --> 13:11.208
Can't be more than ten minutes ahead
of us. We should go, now, and find her.

13:11.583 --> 13:14.962
We're taking him with us.
— and why would we do that?

13:15.045 --> 13:17.673
Because I don't trust him
with anybody but me.

13:21.010 --> 13:22.261
All right, listen up.

13:22.344 --> 13:24.680
I need all of you
to head back to the beach.

13:24.763 --> 13:26.140
When these people show up,

13:26.223 --> 13:29.476
we want to make sure
we're real easy for them to find, ok?

13:29.560 --> 13:31.770
Yeah. — you look worried, Jack.

13:34.273 --> 13:37.359
The only thing I'm worried about
is missing our ride home.

13:42.698 --> 13:45.826
I found her trail. She's headed west
across the island.

13:46.702 --> 13:49.705
Rousseau already found it.
We're going after her now.

13:50.956 --> 13:53.876
But... are you sure it's hers?

13:53.959 --> 13:56.003
Unless someone else is bleeding.

13:56.086 --> 13:59.840
If she didn't want us to find her,
she could've created a dummy trail.

13:59.923 --> 14:02.176
I think we should follow both...
— Kate.

14:02.259 --> 14:05.054
Six hours from now,
we're gonna be sitting on that boat,

14:05.137 --> 14:09.308
laughing about the fact there was
one final thing we couldn't agree upon.

14:09.933 --> 14:12.061
Naomi is hurt. She ran into the jungle.

14:12.144 --> 14:14.646
She's not thinking about
leaving fake trails.

14:16.190 --> 14:18.400
You're right.
— I'll track her down.

14:18.484 --> 14:20.778
Why don't you get everybody
back to the beach?

14:20.861 --> 14:23.405
You got it. — [sighs]

14:30.954 --> 14:32.331
Be careful, ok?

14:45.928 --> 14:49.723
What the hell's gotten into you, Hugo?
They'll all be back in the morning.

14:49.807 --> 14:52.142
We just wait.
— you don't wait with warnings.

14:52.226 --> 14:53.352
You warn.

15:05.989 --> 15:08.909
Here I was thinking I was gonna get
a good night's sleep.

15:19.044 --> 15:20.629
You almost got me that time.

15:20.712 --> 15:23.632
How about best out of seven?

15:24.591 --> 15:26.718
Are you ready for your meds, Hugo?

15:28.387 --> 15:30.597
By the way, you have a visitor.

15:41.608 --> 15:42.943
Mr. Reyes.

15:45.195 --> 15:49.408
My name is Matthew abbadon.
I'm an attorney for oceanic airlines.

15:51.076 --> 15:52.828
Can we talk for a few minutes?

16:01.253 --> 16:06.300
I'm here, Mr. Reyes, 'cause we heard
about your recent... episode.

16:06.967 --> 16:10.053
Your arrest, your incarceration here.

16:11.263 --> 16:13.724
Frankly, we feel terrible about it.

16:14.975 --> 16:17.352
So, on behalf of oceanic,

16:17.436 --> 16:20.522
I'd like to extend you an invitation
for a little upgrade.

16:21.982 --> 16:24.276
What kind of upgrade?

16:26.278 --> 16:29.448
To a facility where the paint
isn't peeling off the walls.

16:30.407 --> 16:33.702
Where you'd have your own bathroom.
You can see the ocean...

16:33.785 --> 16:35.579
I don't want to see the ocean.

16:37.539 --> 16:38.707
No problem.

16:41.668 --> 16:45.464
Actually, thanks. I'm fine right here.

16:47.132 --> 16:49.718
Are you fine, Mr. Reyes?

16:50.886 --> 16:51.970
What do you mean?

16:52.679 --> 16:54.348
You're in a mental institution.

16:56.433 --> 16:58.352
Who'd you say you were again?

16:59.436 --> 17:01.897
I'd like to see a business card.

17:06.985 --> 17:08.987
I must have left them at home.

17:11.240 --> 17:13.033
Then we're done, dude.

17:14.451 --> 17:16.286
Are they still alive?

17:22.376 --> 17:23.543
You heard me.

17:24.586 --> 17:26.755
Nurse! Nurse!

17:26.838 --> 17:28.966
Get out of here!
You better get out of here!

17:29.049 --> 17:31.301
Help me! He's after me!
No, no, no!

17:31.385 --> 17:33.679
That guy's after me. Help me.
— ok, ok.

17:52.364 --> 17:53.991
All right there, Hugo?

17:54.074 --> 17:55.867
Yeah, dude, I'm fine.

17:57.494 --> 17:59.955
You want to talk about it?
— talk about what?

18:00.038 --> 18:01.498
Charlie.

18:06.878 --> 18:10.841
I mean, you two were buddies.
I just thought...

18:12.217 --> 18:15.220
We'll probably get to Jack faster
if we don't talk.

18:22.519 --> 18:24.980
I'm gonna head up
and tell them to slow down.

18:25.063 --> 18:27.357
- — I can keep up.
- All right, ese.

18:27.441 --> 18:30.861
Just... holler if you need me.

19:02.809 --> 19:04.144
Guys!

19:04.811 --> 19:06.146
Guys!

19:07.397 --> 19:08.732
Guys!

19:13.487 --> 19:14.738
Guys!

19:20.452 --> 19:21.787
Guys!

19:22.746 --> 19:25.457
[Wind howling]

19:28.085 --> 19:31.213
[Voices whispering]

19:47.104 --> 19:48.480
The blood trail ends here.

19:49.439 --> 19:50.440
What do you mean?

19:51.733 --> 19:52.734
It ends.

19:52.818 --> 19:55.278
Are you telling me
she stopped bleeding here?

19:55.362 --> 19:58.657
No. I'm telling you she fooled us
and doubled back.

19:59.366 --> 20:00.617
Better call the boat,

20:00.700 --> 20:03.912
tell them she's getting
a really big bundle of firewood.

20:13.839 --> 20:16.591
Ok, I probably should've told you
I saw her take the phone,

20:16.675 --> 20:18.510
but you'd beat me up, Jack.

20:19.511 --> 20:21.763
I owed you one.
— what are you talking about?

20:21.847 --> 20:24.141
Kate took it when she hugged you.

20:27.144 --> 20:29.980
She found the right trail, too.
You wouldn't listen to her.

20:30.063 --> 20:32.566
So, I guess she's taken matters
into her own hands.

20:32.649 --> 20:36.445
But, look on the bright side, somebody
around here knows what they're doing.

21:00.927 --> 21:02.512
[Sat—phone rings]

21:16.776 --> 21:18.862
Hello? — [George] Who's this?

21:20.864 --> 21:23.158
Uh, his is Kate.
— you with Jack?

21:23.241 --> 21:26.453
No, he's not here.
— where's Naomi?

21:28.663 --> 21:30.123
We're looking for her.

21:30.207 --> 21:32.501
What do you mean,
you're looking for her?

21:37.214 --> 21:38.840
[Gasps]

21:40.884 --> 21:42.511
[Grunting, groaning]

21:45.013 --> 21:46.139
Give me the phone.

21:48.600 --> 21:51.269
Give me the phone.
— Naomi, listen to me.

21:51.353 --> 21:54.272
You're hurt, let me help you.
— help me?

21:54.356 --> 21:58.401
I just spent the last three days
trying to get you people rescued,

21:58.485 --> 22:00.529
and you throw this knife in my back.

22:00.612 --> 22:02.489
No, no. That was not us.

22:03.365 --> 22:05.242
Who? — his name is John Locke.

22:06.284 --> 22:08.703
Why?
— he said you weren't who you said.

22:08.787 --> 22:10.956
[Sat—phone rings]

22:11.039 --> 22:14.209
I swear to god we would
never hurt you. You know us.

22:14.960 --> 22:17.420
Please. We need your help.
Please help us.

22:17.504 --> 22:19.506
Give me the phone.

22:25.387 --> 22:27.764
George, it's Naomi.

22:27.847 --> 22:31.393
Naomi, where have you been?
What's going on over there?

22:34.145 --> 22:37.524
I had an accident. I'm hurt.

22:37.607 --> 22:41.194
An accident? What accident?
What happened?

22:42.404 --> 22:43.863
Naomi.

22:44.823 --> 22:45.824
Hello?

22:46.324 --> 22:48.994
Hello. — I hit a tree branch...

22:49.828 --> 22:51.496
When I parachuted in.

22:52.080 --> 22:53.415
Took it through my gut.

22:53.498 --> 22:55.875
Why did they tell me
you were getting firewood?

22:55.959 --> 22:59.671
I guess they were afraid to tell you
what happened till I could talk to you.

22:59.754 --> 23:02.757
We've lost our signal,
and we can't come get you.

23:02.841 --> 23:05.010
Can you change
your tracking frequency?

23:10.307 --> 23:11.766
Try it now.

23:12.434 --> 23:13.893
Clear as a bell.

23:13.977 --> 23:17.772
Hang on, Naomi, we'll get you
back here asap, ok?

23:17.856 --> 23:20.066
I'm sorry, George.

23:22.193 --> 23:24.654
Just tell my sister that I love her.

23:25.697 --> 23:26.740
[Phone beeps]

24:02.567 --> 24:04.986
[Creaking]

24:16.706 --> 24:18.208
[Panting]

24:19.834 --> 24:21.044
Help!

24:21.753 --> 24:23.588
Help!

24:23.672 --> 24:24.964
Help!

24:40.313 --> 24:41.940
There's nothing here.

24:42.023 --> 24:43.441
There's nothing here.

24:43.525 --> 24:45.193
There's nothing here.

24:45.276 --> 24:46.986
There's nothing here!

24:56.287 --> 24:58.623
[Screams]

25:00.083 --> 25:01.543
Hello, Hugo.

25:04.045 --> 25:06.589
You've got yourself
good and lost out here, Hugo.

25:09.092 --> 25:11.594
How did you get separated
from the group?

25:15.348 --> 25:16.474
I just...

25:18.351 --> 25:19.894
Fell behind, I guess.

25:19.978 --> 25:22.647
Is that why you were shouting for help?

25:22.731 --> 25:24.399
I got scared.

25:28.278 --> 25:31.239
What Desmond said happened
down in that station,

25:32.031 --> 25:34.242
"not penny's boat."

25:34.826 --> 25:37.579
Are you sure that's what
Charlie wrote on his hand?

25:38.163 --> 25:40.415
Jack should never have called
those people.

25:40.498 --> 25:42.375
I couldn't agree more.

25:44.169 --> 25:47.297
It's gonna be hard
to talk him into thinking

25:47.380 --> 25:49.257
they're not coming here to rescue us.

25:49.340 --> 25:52.510
Well, guess we're gonna have
to try our best, Hugo...

25:53.678 --> 25:56.473
Because if we can't talk him
out of it...

25:58.391 --> 26:00.310
Then Charlie died for nothing.

26:16.618 --> 26:18.411
Where the hell have you been,
Hugo?

26:18.495 --> 26:22.624
Sorry. I was just, uh... I got lost.

26:26.294 --> 26:28.630
[Sawyer sighs]

26:28.713 --> 26:30.507
What are you doing here?

26:31.883 --> 26:34.135
I came here
for the same reason you did,

26:34.219 --> 26:36.471
to warn Jack about the people
on that boat.

26:36.554 --> 26:37.972
I already gave it a shot,

26:38.056 --> 26:41.684
but... ifigured I might have
better luck with some support.

26:42.435 --> 26:43.895
You want my support?

26:43.978 --> 26:46.815
You can tell me why you destroyed
that submarine.

26:48.650 --> 26:50.193
[Guns cock]

26:58.743 --> 27:00.328
[Sun calls to Jin]

27:21.599 --> 27:22.600
[Sighs]

27:24.102 --> 27:25.854
Still in one piece.

27:25.937 --> 27:27.522
Rambo.

27:27.605 --> 27:28.606
[Laughs]

27:28.690 --> 27:30.567
[Chatter]

27:46.708 --> 27:48.877
[Aaron cries]

28:11.816 --> 28:13.818
Charlie's dead.

28:26.873 --> 28:28.875
[Sobs]

28:39.552 --> 28:41.554
I'd watch out if I were you.

28:42.221 --> 28:44.098
What are you talking about, dude?

28:44.182 --> 28:47.352
There's a guy over there,
staring at you.

28:48.186 --> 28:50.521
What guy? — that guy.

28:53.900 --> 28:55.109
Hey, man.

28:56.027 --> 28:57.278
Don't run.

28:58.863 --> 29:01.908
Hurley, just...

29:04.243 --> 29:05.453
Sit down.

29:06.788 --> 29:08.206
I want to talk to you.

29:11.292 --> 29:12.710
Come on.

29:13.544 --> 29:15.797
Don't do what you did in the store, ok?

29:17.048 --> 29:20.385
There's no need to... freak out.

29:20.468 --> 29:23.805
No need to freak out? I'm trying
to buy some jerky and a slushee,

29:23.888 --> 29:26.307
and suddenly you're
standing over by the ho hos.

29:26.391 --> 29:28.476
You're dead.
What do you expect me to do?

29:29.227 --> 29:31.604
Can we just... sit down?

29:32.730 --> 29:35.483
I may be in the mental hospital,
but I know you're dead,

29:35.566 --> 29:38.695
and I'm not having an imaginary
conversation with you.

29:39.946 --> 29:40.989
I am dead.

29:45.076 --> 29:46.744
But I'm also here.

29:48.246 --> 29:49.580
Ok, prove it.

29:58.047 --> 30:00.258
Ok, ok.

30:09.726 --> 30:12.770
Did you know you were going to die
when you swam out there?

30:21.988 --> 30:23.531
Why didn't you tell me?

30:23.614 --> 30:26.117
Because you would've tried to stop me.

30:27.410 --> 30:31.122
And since I was gonna do it anwvay
I thought to spare you all the drama.

30:34.292 --> 30:36.294
And now you have to do something...

30:37.754 --> 30:39.547
But you're hiding from it.

30:41.090 --> 30:44.719
That's the real reason you ran
when you saw me in the store.

30:44.802 --> 30:48.264
You knew I was here to tell you.
— I'm not listening to this.

30:48.890 --> 30:50.308
No, 'cause you're not here.

30:50.391 --> 30:52.185
I am here. You're being a baby.

30:52.268 --> 30:54.562
I'm gonna close my eyes,
and count to five.

30:54.645 --> 30:56.898
When I open them, you'll be gone.
— I am here.

30:56.981 --> 30:58.858
One.. Wo.. — don't do this.

30:58.941 --> 31:00.568
They need you. — ...Three...

31:00.651 --> 31:02.195
They need you. — ...Four...

31:02.278 --> 31:04.155
You know they need you.
— ...Five!

31:20.379 --> 31:23.132
When? What happened?

31:25.968 --> 31:28.596
I mean, how did he...?

31:31.057 --> 31:33.643
He was trying to help us.

31:50.701 --> 31:53.287
[Grunts]

31:55.540 --> 31:58.751
[Groans, panting]

32:05.216 --> 32:06.551
[Gun cocks]

32:15.476 --> 32:17.270
You're not gonna shoot me, Jack...

32:18.437 --> 32:21.065
Any more than I was gonna shoot...
— [gun clicks]

32:24.861 --> 32:26.487
It's not loaded.

32:33.578 --> 32:35.997
Come on, Jack. — let go of me!

32:39.375 --> 32:41.836
Do you know what he did?
— yes, I know what he did!

32:41.919 --> 32:43.421
[Locke] All I did...

32:44.589 --> 32:47.091
All I have ever done...

32:47.717 --> 32:49.969
Has been in the best interest
of all of us.

32:50.052 --> 32:51.596
Are you insane?

32:56.100 --> 32:58.686
I know,
I have a lot of explaining to do,

32:58.769 --> 33:03.065
but I never did anything
to hurt any of you.

33:03.149 --> 33:06.569
I even risked my life to tell you
that there was a traitor in your midst.

33:06.652 --> 33:07.778
She helped us, John.

33:07.862 --> 33:10.781
All you ever did was blow up
every chance we had

33:10.865 --> 33:12.700
of getting off this island.

33:12.783 --> 33:14.368
You killed Naomi!

33:14.452 --> 33:17.371
Well, technically,
he didn't kill her yet.

33:17.455 --> 33:19.248
[Kate] Yes, he did.

33:22.210 --> 33:23.669
She just died.

33:24.879 --> 33:26.339
She didn't give you up, John.

33:26.422 --> 33:30.009
She covered for us, and she fixed this.

33:30.092 --> 33:31.427
They're on their way.

33:33.387 --> 33:35.181
She didn't cover for anyone.

33:35.264 --> 33:38.726
She wants her people to come here.

33:39.268 --> 33:42.396
And trust me, when they do,
we had better be far away from here.

33:43.981 --> 33:46.692
I'm going to the barracks.
The others abandoned them.

33:46.776 --> 33:49.654
It's the only place on the island
with any form of security.

33:49.737 --> 33:52.156
It'll have to do until
I think of something else.

33:53.324 --> 33:55.785
Until then, if you want to live...

33:56.661 --> 33:58.120
You need to come with me.

33:59.580 --> 34:01.916
No one's going anwvhere
with you, John,

34:01.999 --> 34:04.669
because they're not crazy.
— he's not crazy.

34:06.170 --> 34:07.922
What about Charlie?

34:11.008 --> 34:14.804
Charlie went down to that place
so we could all be rescued.

34:20.935 --> 34:23.854
And whatever he did down there,
it worked.

34:27.275 --> 34:29.443
But then something
must have happened...

34:31.737 --> 34:34.198
Must've heard something before he...

34:39.412 --> 34:42.790
I don't know why,
but he changed his mind.

34:50.089 --> 34:52.675
Because the last thing he did
was to warn us

34:52.758 --> 34:55.761
that the people on that boat
are not who they said they were.

34:57.555 --> 34:59.932
[Mouths] Not penny's boat.

35:10.901 --> 35:12.695
So I'm not listening to you.

35:16.574 --> 35:18.784
I'm listening to my friend.

35:22.538 --> 35:24.248
I'm listening to Charlie.

35:38.929 --> 35:40.181
Anyone else?

35:44.268 --> 35:45.811
There isn't much time.

36:00.618 --> 36:03.788
Jack, with your permission,
I'd like to go with John.

36:08.292 --> 36:09.794
He's all yours.

36:19.637 --> 36:22.139
[Quiet chatter]

36:25.643 --> 36:27.561
You said we'd never leave the island.

36:27.645 --> 36:31.565
If you want to go with Locke,
I'll be right behind you.

36:32.400 --> 36:34.443
I'm not going anwvhere with that man.

36:45.162 --> 36:46.497
What are you doing?

36:52.169 --> 36:54.755
Same thing I've always done, Kate.

36:55.881 --> 36:57.216
Surviving.

37:02.346 --> 37:06.350
Fihundefl

37:18.487 --> 37:21.365
You know where to find us
when you change your mind.

38:07.745 --> 38:08.996
You ever miss?

38:15.377 --> 38:19.798
Yeah. I was on my way back
from a consult.

38:19.882 --> 38:22.051
Thought I'd drop by and pay you a visit.

38:24.595 --> 38:25.846
Horse?

38:25.930 --> 38:27.348
You're on.

38:29.183 --> 38:30.851
So consult, huh?

38:30.935 --> 38:33.854
Does that mean you're back
doing surgical stuff?

38:43.239 --> 38:45.032
[Hugo] Reporters leaving you alone?

38:49.870 --> 38:52.873
Still have to sign some autographs
when I go out for coffee.

38:54.583 --> 38:56.252
Thinking about growing a beard.

38:59.547 --> 39:01.423
You'd look weird with a beard, dude.

39:02.841 --> 39:03.842
That's h—o.

39:09.265 --> 39:11.433
What are you really doing here, Jack?

39:16.021 --> 39:19.316
I was just checking on you,
seeing if everything was ok.

39:20.484 --> 39:22.570
You're checking to see if I went nuts,

39:22.653 --> 39:24.738
if I was gonna tell.

39:26.824 --> 39:28.158
Are you?

39:33.122 --> 39:34.331
You're up.

39:37.376 --> 39:39.378
No, you win. I...

39:42.131 --> 39:43.632
I gotta run.

39:46.135 --> 39:47.803
It was great seeing you, Hurley.

39:54.393 --> 39:55.853
I'm sorry.

40:01.692 --> 40:03.861
I'm sorry I went with Locke.

40:06.780 --> 40:08.782
I should've stayed with you.

40:10.743 --> 40:12.870
It's water under the bridge, man.

40:18.876 --> 40:21.170
I don't think we did
the right thing, Jack.

40:22.546 --> 40:24.673
I think it wants us to come back.
— Hurley.

40:24.757 --> 40:27.760
It's gonna do everything it...
— we're never going back!

40:38.646 --> 40:40.314
Never say never, dude.

41:04.421 --> 41:06.131
Are you thinking of Charlie?

41:07.508 --> 41:10.511
Feels like a hundred years ago
we came out here together.

41:13.263 --> 41:15.140
How did this happen?

41:15.224 --> 41:17.267
Fihundefl

41:24.274 --> 41:27.111
Thunder's getting louder.

41:27.194 --> 41:29.822
[Helicopter whirring]

41:31.490 --> 41:33.117
That's not thunder.

41:33.200 --> 41:34.702
Come on.

41:45.879 --> 41:47.506
Come on.

42:13.157 --> 42:14.575
Are you Jack?
